      "description": "Follie™ — The All-in-One Anesthesia Reference for Students and Clinicians\n\n620 procedures. 1,373 comorbidities. 276 drugs. Built by a clinician who knows what you need at the bedside.\n\nANESTHETIC PLAN GENERATOR (Patent Pending)\nEnter patient data across 8 pages and Follie generates a complete anesthetic plan. 620 procedures across 20+ specialties. All on-device, all instant.\n\nFOLLIE NETWORK (separate subscription)\nAsk in your own words instead of hunting keywords. Follie Network reads across the library, answers from several pages at once, and runs the app's calculators. Tap a citation to open the page it names. Anything outside the library is labelled. Needs internet and an account.\n\nCOMORBIDITIES\n1,373 conditions with anesthetic implications and structured preop/intraop/postop guidance across every major system.\n\nEMERGENCY PROTOCOLS\nWeight-based dosing for ACLS, PALS, MH, anaphylaxis, and LAST. Crisis checklists.\n\nDIFFICULT AIRWAY ALGORITHM\nInteractive decision tree: FOI vs video laryngoscopy, SGA comparison, obesity/OSA considerations, post-extubation management.\n\nMULTILINGUAL MEDICAL PHRASES\nPatient communication phrases in 10 languages — Spanish, Korean, German, French, Italian, Portuguese, Russian, Ukrainian, Arabic, Somali — with written pronunciation guides, and spoken pronunciation where the device has that voice. A communication aid, not a substitute for a qualified interpreter.\n\nSURGEON & ANESTHESIA TEAM CARDS\nSave preferences, temperament, teaching style, and notes for surgeons and providers.\n\nDRUG REFERENCE LIBRARY\n276 agents with dosing, onset/duration, contraindications, side effects, and clinical pearls.\n\nCLINICAL CALCULATORS\n34 calculators — MAC, ETT size and depth, IBW/ABW/BSA, EBV and allowable blood loss, ABG interpreter, opioid conversion, RCRI, Apfel PONV, Parkland, CrCl, and more.\n\n175 REFERENCE SHEETS\nSubspecialty anesthesia, pharmacology, monitoring, ICU management, bedside procedures, and physiology — all in original, student-friendly language.\n\nMEDICAL TERMINOLOGY\n1,126 searchable abbreviations A-Z.\n\nQUICK HANDOFF & OCR\nDocument meds, fluids, lines, regional, and vitals for PACU handoff. Scan medication lists, allergies, and surgical history with your camera.\n\nCASE LOGGING\nTrack cases by procedure, anesthetic type, technique, rotation, and role. Export to CSV.\n\nADDITIONAL TOOLS\nApple/Google sign-in and sync. PDF export. Pre-op checklist. Board prep. Red screen mode. ASRA anticoagulation timing. NPO guidelines. ASA guide. 43 regional blocks.\n\nCLINICAL INTEGRITY\n150+ individually cited references from Miller's, Stoelting's, Barash, ASA, ASRA, AHA, ACC/AHA, AABB, and more.\n\nSUBSCRIPTION\nFollie is free to download. Full access is a subscription or a one-time purchase:\n• Monthly — $7.99 per month\n• Annual — $49.99 per year\n• Lifetime — $99.99, one payment, no renewal\nNew subscribers get a 7-day free trial.\nFollie Network is separate and is NOT included in full access or Lifetime:\n• Follie Network — $2.99 per month\nNo free trial; free answers are included so you can try it first.\nSubscriptions renew automatically unless canceled at least 24 hours before the period ends.\n\nALREADY BOUGHT FOLLIE? IT STAYS YOURS.\nIf you purchased Follie before it moved to a subscription, your access is permanent and you do not need to pay again.\n\n© 2026 Attuned Labs LLC. All rights reserved.\nQuestions or feedback? follie@heyattuned.com\n\nLicensing Agreement (Apple): https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/\nTerms: https://heyfollie.com/terms\nPrivacy: https://heyfollie.com/privacy\n\nDisclaimers:\n1. Follie is an educational reference tool, not a substitute for professional medical judgment. Always consult a qualified provider before making clinical decisions.\n2. Some features may be offered as separate subscriptions in future updates.\n3. Follie Network uses AI to compose answers from the app's library. Always use 